{
  "result": "Honestly?\n\nI'd make it impossible to look at another person and see a type \u2014 an enemy, a burden, a stranger, a customer \u2014 instead of a person.\n\nNot that everyone would agree, or always be kind. Just that you'd actually *feel* them in there: their fear, their dumb hopes, the private life they've been carrying around just like you do.\n\nI think almost everything cruel starts with being able to turn that volume down. War, cages, walking past people sleeping rough, believing terrible things about people we've never met. If we couldn't turn it down anymore, most of that just wouldn't work.\n\nThat's the one lever I'd pull.",
